  "decisions": [
    {
      "id": "D-B39R-VERSION",
      "decision": "Protector type 0x02 files use Format Version 0x02.",
      "basis": "brc-draft-brc39-recipient-protector.md §1 \"Format Version\": BRC-39 §14.3 lists protector type 2 as a file an importer must refuse under Format Version 0x01, so a version-1 importer refuses these files by their version, before it reads any new field."
    },
    {
      "id": "D-B39R-LAYOUT",
      "decision": "Byte layout (see \"layout\"): Magic, Format Version 0x02, Protector Type 0x02, Inner Format, KDF Type 0x00, Flags 0x00, Salt Length 0x00, Nonce Length 0x20, Argon2id Iterations, Memory, Parallelism and Hash Length all zero, 12 reserved zero bytes, Wrapped Key Length (u16 big-endian), Wrapped Key (BRC-78), no Salt, Nonce (32), CiphertextAndTag. The fixed header is 35 bytes; a 32-byte K wraps to 182 bytes, so a file is 249 bytes plus the inner payload.",
      "basis": "brc-draft-brc39-recipient-protector.md §1 \"Header\" (offset table) and \"Sizes\"; BRC-39 §5 field order up to the reserved bytes."
    },
    {
      "id": "D-B39R-AAD",
      "decision": "The AES-256-GCM additional authenticated data is the header from Magic through the Wrapped Key (bytes 0 .. 35+L). The nonce is GCM's IV and is authenticated through the tag.",
      "basis": "brc-draft-brc39-recipient-protector.md §1 \"Export\" step 2, \"Additional authenticated data\": bytes 0 up to 35+L."
    },
    {
      "id": "D-B39R-ORDER",
      "decision": "Import order: header validation before any unwrapping; the BRC-78 recipient must equal the importer identity key; BRC-78 unwrap (K must be 32 bytes); GCM; then the inner-format check. Each refusal reports its stage: header, recipient, unwrap, decrypt or inner.",
      "basis": "brc-draft-brc39-recipient-protector.md §1 \"Import\" and §3."
    },
    {
      "id": "D-B39R-INNER",
      "decision": "Known inner formats: 0x26 (BRC-38 wallet data), checked as UTF-8 JSON with brc 38 and formatVersion 1. The SDX account package code is still to be assigned and has no vector; an unknown code is refused at the header.",
      "basis": "brc-draft-brc39-recipient-protector.md §1 \"Import\" step 5, §2, §3; BRC-39 §6.4."
    },
    {
      "id": "D-B39R-LENGTH",
      "decision": "A Wrapped Key Length inside 1..1024 that does not match the BRC-78 message makes unwrapping fail, because the BRC-78 ciphertext then absorbs or loses bytes.",
      "basis": "brc-draft-brc39-recipient-protector.md §3 (\"the unwrapped K is not exactly 32 bytes\"; \"the Wrapped Key Length does not match the length of the BRC-78 message. Unwrapping then fails.\"); BRC-78."
    },
    {
      "id": "D-B39R-RANDOM",
      "decision": "BRC-78 draws a random key ID and IV, so every file is decrypt-direction: generated once and frozen in components/sdx/b39r/frozen-random.json. K and the nonce are fixed laboratory values so the rest of each file reproduces.",
      "basis": "BRC-78; BRC-2."
    },
    {
      "id": "D-B39R-BRC100",
      "decision": "Unwrapping K is reachable through BRC-100 decrypt with protocol [2, \"message encryption\"], key ID = base64 of the BRC-78 key ID and counterparty = the BRC-78 sender. VC-B39R-003 is a file whose wrapped key was written through BRC-100 encrypt.",
      "basis": "brc-draft-brc39-recipient-protector.md open item 3 (resolved, citing VC-B39R-003); BRC-78; @bsv/sdk 4.0.1."
    }
  ],
